Comment (main.go:185):
This should be a Component
Replies:
I think this is already modeled correctly. These templates describe the per-resource ELBv2 subjects (`aws-elbv2-loadbalancer`, listener, target group, and target health), which are emitted as inventory items. The component subject is emitted separately as `common-components/aws-elbv2` via `defaultComponents()` and `subjectsForRecord()`, and each inventory item links back to it through `ImplementedComponents`, so changing this helper to `SUBJECT_TYPE_COMPONENT` would incorrectly make every ELBv2 resource a component.
You are wrong :). We need to make every ELBv2 resource a component so API treats this Subject Template as automation for automatic creation of component definitions (and further automation of system components). You can check the API code `https://github.com/compliance-framework/api` if you need help verifying that I am actually correct and this needs fixing.
Implementation guidance: Update the ELBv2 resource subject modeling so the four resource templates are components, as directed by the reviewer. In main.go, change subjectTemplate so the returned proto.SubjectTemplate uses Type: proto.SubjectType_SUBJECT_TYPE_COMPONENT instead of SUBJECT_TYPE_INVENTORY_ITEM. In input.go, update buildResourceRecord so ResourceRecord.SubjectType is proto.SubjectType_SUBJECT_TYPE_COMPONENT for load balancer, listener, target-group, and target-health records; this keeps subjectsForRecord emitting the resource subject with the same type as the registered template. Preserve the existing common component from defaultComponents() and the existing inventoryForRecord() inventory item with ImplementedComponents linking to common-components/aws-elbv2 unless tests or API types force a narrower adjustment. Add or update tests/assertions that Init registers all four aws-elbv2-* subject templates as components and that generated per-resource subjects use SUBJECT_TYPE_COMPONENT. Avoid changing resource IDs, subject identifiers, policy behavior routing, or inventory item identifiers.
